WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
Venice, at night.

2
00:00:02.110 --> 00:00:04.360
Armed men surround a general.

3
00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:05.630
He doesn't draw.

4
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.600
He says: "Keep up your bright
swords, for the dew will rust them."

5
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:11.860
Act 5.

6
00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.620
The same man stands
beside a curtained bed,

7
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:16.410
facing three officials.

8
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:20.590
He has one request: "Speak of me as I am."

9
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.240
Is this the noble general back at last?

10
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.770
Or a man hiding from what he did?

11
00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:29.270
In this mission, you'll hear
the grand voice of Act 1.

12
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.370
Bradley called him "the
greatest poet of them all".

13
00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.450
You'll watch that voice
break apart in Act 4.

14
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.440
And you'll meet critics
who split sharply over him:

15
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:41.530
Bradley, Eliot, Leavis and Gardner.

16
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.120
Your mission: decide whether the
last speech is noble, or hiding.
